diagnostic_evidence.quote:
Since $V^\lambda$ is a viscosity supersolution of the penalized PDE, we have
\begin{equation}
\label{T5:1}
-\mathcal{L}\psi(t_0,x_0)-f_\lambda\bigl(t_0,x_0,\psi(t_0,x_0),\sigma(t_0,x_0)\nabla_x\psi(t_0,x_0)\bigr)\ge 0.

failure_location.quote:
the viscosity supersolution property of $V^\lambda$ yields
\begin{equation}\label{eq:viscsuper}
\mathcal{L}\phi(t_0,x_0)+f_\lambda\bigl(t_0,x_0,\phi(t_0,x_0),\sigma(t_0,x_0)\nabla\phi(t_0,x_0)\bigr)\ge 0.

In particular, if $\lambda=\Delta t^{-\frac{1}{2}}$, we obtain the minimal error rate
$$\left(\max_{i\in\{0,\cdots,n-1\}}\mathbb{E}\left|Y_{t_i}-\mathcal{Y}^{\lambda,\pi}_{t_i}\right|^2\right)^{\frac{1}{2}}
        \le C_2 \Delta t^\frac{1}{4}$$
